# Fixtures are inputs to a parser, so their bytes are the test.
#
# `Fixtures/issues/adversarial.md` carries CRLF line endings deliberately —
# `IssueMarkdownParserTests` asserts the parser survives them. Git's default
# text handling normalised those 17 CRLF pairs to LF on the way into the object
# store, so the fixture kept its CRLF only in the working copy where it was
# written: a fresh clone got pure LF, and the assertion passed while testing
# nothing. `-text` disables that conversion, so what the test reads is what was
# committed.
Fixtures/** -text
